  "description": "<p>GET on test/fcr:metadata/fcr:acl on a binary resource fails with a 400.  So does test/fcr:versions/fcr:acl return 400.  </p>\n\n<p>These endpoints should return 404 since they do not exist. </p>\n\n<p> </p>\n\n<p> </p>\n<div class=\"code panel\" style=\"border-width: 1px;\"><div class=\"codeContent panelContent\">\n<pre class=\"code-java\">\r\n#To reproduce: \r\n#Create a binary resource:\r\ncurl -u fedoraAdmin:fedoraAdmin http:<span class=\"code-comment\">//localhost:8080/<span class=\"code-keyword\">rest</span>/test -X PUT  -H <span class=\"code-quote\">\"Content-Type:text/plain\"</span> -d <span class=\"code-quote\">\"test\"</span>\r\n</span>#Get the metadata: \r\ncurl -u fedoraAdmin:fedoraAdmin http:<span class=\"code-comment\">//localhost:8080/<span class=\"code-keyword\">rest</span>/test/fcr:metadata -i\r\n</span>#See the <span class=\"code-quote\">\"acl\"</span> link? No <span class=\"code-keyword\">try</span> to get it and verify the 400\r\ncurl -u fedoraAdmin:fedoraAdmin http:<span class=\"code-comment\">//localhost:8080/<span class=\"code-keyword\">rest</span>/test/fcr:metadata/fcr:acl -i  \r\n</span>#Same with versions endpoint:\r\ncurl -u fedoraAdmin:fedoraAdmin http:<span class=\"code-comment\">//localhost:8080/<span class=\"code-keyword\">rest</span>/test/fcr:versions/fcr:acl -i      \r\n</span>curl -u fedoraAdmin:fedoraAdmin http:<span class=\"code-comment\">//localhost:8080/<span class=\"code-keyword\">rest</span>/test/fcr:metadata/fcr:versions/fcr:acl -i   \r\n</span>#Same is <span class=\"code-keyword\">true</span> <span class=\"code-keyword\">for</span> container/fcr:versions/fcr:acl\r\n#Same is <span class=\"code-keyword\">true</span> <span class=\"code-keyword\">for</span> PUTs on the above acl resources.</pre>\n</div></div>\n<p> </p>\n\n<p> </p>\n\n<p> </p>\n\n<p> </p>",
